        <mxCell id="note_title" value="MODELING DECISIONS TO REVIEW" style="text;html=1;fontColor=#0f172a;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="840" y="470" width="320" height="36" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="• Surrogate keys are deterministic hashes, not sequences, so reruns and backfills leave existing facts valid.&lt;br&gt;• Source order lines are deduplicated in staging before the fact is built.&lt;br&gt;• customer_key resolves the SCD2 version valid at order time: order_placed_at between valid_from and valid_to.&lt;br&gt;• unit_price and cost_amount are frozen on the fact. dim_product holds current prices only and overwrites.&lt;br&gt;• line_total = quantity × unit_price − discount_amount.&lt;br&gt;• No fct_orders in v1, so shipping_cost and order_total stay out of marts. The header-vs-lines test lives in staging.&lt;br&gt;• order_status is carried so cancelled and returned orders can be excluded. Decide the eligible set before publishing revenue.&lt;br&gt;• dim_payment omitted; payment_method would be a degenerate column if needed." style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#eff6ff;strokeColor=#93c5fd;fontColor=#193252;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="840" y="507" width="340" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="footer" value="Source context: customers, products, orders, order_items. This is a proposed analytical design—not a deployed Snowflake schema." style="text;html=1;fontColor=#64748b;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="940" width="1140" height="42" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
